Install:
    tested on python=3.10, CUDA=12.1, pytorch=2.6

    pip install torch=2.6 torchvision=0.21 torchaudio=2.6
    pip install -re requirements.txt
    pip install -e .

    cd HRI_mllm/external/HRI_retarget
    git checkout g1_hri_mllm(maybe not need this line?)


    pip install -e .

    you may need to install egl:
    sudo apt-get install libegl1-mesa-dev


Compute joint_vec:
    python HRI_mllm/external/HRI_retarget/HRI_retarget/scripts/g1ml3d_motion_representation.py 
    python HRI_mllm/external/HRI_retarget/HRI_retarget/utils/io/inspirehand_mean_variance.py

    remember to change path in /root/pengyang/codebase/HRI_MLLM/HRI_mllm/utils/motion_utils/g1ml3d.py
    copy texts folder


Train motion VQVAE:
    python HRI_mllm/train/train_vae.py
    TODO: fix /root/pengyang/codebase/HRI_MLLM/HRI_mllm/datasets/G1ML3D.py remove all cfg dependency

VQVAE:
    python HRI_mllm/scripts/test_motion_encoder.py


Generate tokens for dataset:
    python HRI_mllm/datasets/BEAT_preprocess/generate_tokens.py



Train motion adaptor:
    generate motion tokens first:
        python HRI_mllm/scripts/generate_motion_tokens.py

    then 
        python -m torch.distributed.launch --nproc_per_node=8 --nnodes=1 --node_rank=0 \
            HRI_mllm/train/train_motion_adaptor.py 


Test motion adaptor:
    CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python HRI_mllm/test/test_gpt2_adaptor.py
    ### TODO: now audio_tokenizer seems to be loaded on the wrong device.

Inference with gpt2 motion adaptor:
    CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0,1 python HRI_mllm/scripts/test_qwen2_5omni_motion_full.py 


After change llm model, create a randomized base model based on kimi-audio-7b-instruct:
    python HRI_mllm/model/kimi_motion/create_base_model.py

Create finetune dataset:
    python HRI_mllm/datasets/BEAT_preprocess/create_jsonl.py

CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python /root/pengyang/codebase/HRI_MLLM/HRI_mllm/train/finetune_kimi_motion.py \
    --model_name_or_path "output/motion_model/Kimi-Audio-Motion-7B" \
    --model_path "output/motion_model/Kimi-Audio-Motion-7B" \
    --data_path "/root/pengyang/codebase/HRI_MLLM/data/BEAT_v1_kimi/beat_v1_full.jsonl" \
    --eval_ratio 0.05 \
    --bf16 True \
    --output_dir output/kimiaudio_ckpts \
    --num_train_epochs 5 \
    --per_device_train_batch_size 1 \
    --per_device_eval_batch_size 1 \
    --gradient_accumulation_steps 1 \
    --eval_strategy "no" \
    --save_strategy "steps" \
    --save_steps 1000 \
    --save_total_limit 10 \
    --learning_rate 1e-5 \
    --weight_decay 0.1 \
    --adam_beta2 0.95 \
    --warmup_ratio 0.01 \
    --lr_scheduler_type "cosine" \
    --logging_steps 1 \
    --report_to "none" \
    --model_max_length 512 \
    --gradient_checkpointing True \
    --lazy_preprocess True \
    --deepspeed /root/pengyang/codebase/HRI_MLLM/HRI_mllm/finetune/ds_config_zero3.json


3. Finetune the model.

    You can use the following command to finetune the model.

    ```bash
    bash HRI_mllm/finetune/finetune_ds.sh \
        --model_path "output/motion_model/Kimi-Audio-Motion-7B" \
        --data "/root/pengyang/codebase/HRI_MLLM/data/BEAT_v1_kimi/beat_v1_full.jsonl"
    ```

4. Convert the finetuned model for inference.
    ```bash
    CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python -m finetune_codes.model --model_name "moonshotai/Kimi-Audio-7B" \
    --action "export_model" \
    --input_dir "output/kimiaudio_ckpts" \
    --output_dir "output/finetuned_hf_for_inference"
    ```

You can infer with the finetuned model by running:
    ```bash
    CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python -m finetune_codes.check_sft_infer
    ```

Server:
    python HRI_mllm/inference/text_response_server.py

    # visit http://localhost:5000/response?text=your_text_here

    # or use curl
    # curl -X GET "http://localhost:5000/response?text=your_text_here"



